**EMPTY RESULTS: the nudge names the wrong hypothesis.** Live sighting #2 (the
first is recorded in `locode/tools/shell.py`'s own comment, at six consecutive
empty git queries). Observed run: 8 iterations, 7 tool calls, 4 nudges, stopped.

    bash git ls-tree -r --name-only main https://github.com/google/skills.git skills/cloud
      -> exit 0, no output
    [nudge: every call returning empty]
    bash git ls-tree -r --name-only main https://github.com/google/skills.git | head -30
      -> exit 0, no output
    [stopped: every tool call kept coming back empty]

**All the machinery fired correctly. The CONTENT of the nudge is what failed.**
`_nudge_no_information` (loop.py:1876) says the fault is "the **path, the ref,
the directory, the pattern or the repo** you are asking about" — every item is
about the TARGET. The real fault was the COMMAND: `git ls-tree` reads the local
object database and cannot take a URL at all, so the URL was parsed as a
pathspec. The model then did the most reasonable thing the nudge allowed — drop
the `skills/cloud` pathspec — which could never work. **Verified 2026-08-15 in a
scratch repo: `git ls-tree -r --name-only main <URL>` exits 0 with ZERO output
even with no pathspec at all.** The nudge's remedies ("list the parent
directory, list the whole tree") are also unreachable here: they presuppose a
local repo and nothing was ever cloned.

**Missing hypothesis: "the command itself cannot answer this question."** For
git it is a sharp class — `ls-tree`/`log`/`show`/`cat-file` are local-only;
`ls-remote`/`clone`/`fetch`/`archive --remote` take URLs — and handing a URL to
the first group is SILENTLY EMPTY rather than an error, the worst possible
signal.

**CHOSEN SURFACE — the tool RESULT, not the nudge text.** Have `bash` detect a
local-only git subcommand handed a URL-shaped argument and return that specific
fact instead of the generic `_EMPTY_OK` (shell.py:29). Rationale, from this
repo's own history: 0b-iii — six builds of rewriting the MESSAGE moved nothing,
one sentence in the tool DESCRIPTION moved 7/24 -> 22/24 ("I have been tuning
the wrong surface"). **REJECTED alternative: widening the nudge text**, because
resume item 0b closes that surface — this model obeys whichever demand the
sentence leads with and only that one, so a second hypothesis likely just swaps
which one gets obeyed; the fix must REMOVE a demand, not re-rank it.

Scope honestly: this fixes git-with-a-URL, NOT "empty because the command was
wrong" in general. The general version is unreachable.

